  "reveal": {
    "brief_voiced": "The killer was Lady Lavinia Loveless. The touch faltered twice. Fides tripped about the first minute of the touch; the green hand's own trip — a new hand's stumble convicts nobody, and the tower thinks no worse of it. But Patientia hung late where the method wanted her elsewhere, and no custom excuses it; that rope was in Lady Lavinia Loveless's keeping, and the hands that should have held it were free about the third minute of the touch. Zane Swain did not survive the office.\n\nAs to the why of it: Of Lady Lavinia Loveless, the playbill says: Lady Lavinia Loveless — a faded actress turned medium; apt to let people rather too close. Of Zane Swain: Zane Swain — a footman, twin to Fifi; correct in all things, fond of the rules.\n\nThe tower proved every pair of hands but one.",
